  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 115 AM CDT Sun Aug 23 2026\n\nThe ridge will begin to weaken slightly and shift west \nTuesday/Wednesday, but not before another couple of very hot days. \nNorthwesterly flow will develop aloft allowing storms that develop \nover northern NM to move toward the area late Wednesday. Confidence \nis slightly higher for more widespread coverage of storms so rain \nchances have increased to 30-40% for SE NM and the northern Permian \nBasin. More storms are possible Thursday which could keep \ntemperatures under 100 for some locations, but won't pull the \ntrigger on that yet. Drier conditions return late week with \ntemperatures remaining well above normal.",
